#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1063 expect=noViolation domain=AE
#note "Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner 2026-10-04: \"Agree to case insensitive compare using upper if needed.\"): the datasets arrive named in lower case (ae, vs), as a provider that passes a file name through unchanged would hand them over; the Define-XML declares AE and VS. define_dataset_names() is upper-cased by the engine, so the rule upper-cases ds_name() too and must not fire. Before upper(ds_name()) the raw 'ae' was not in [AE, VS] and fired."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#define-xml PMDA-SD1063-define-both.xml
dataset ae label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE
---

dataset vs label="Vital Signs"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
---
S1 | VS | 001 | 1 | SYSBP
